# $_ with dot access: $_.age desugars to [fn [_] $_.age] via WRAP-CALL.
# Verifies the implicit lambda works correctly when passed to $map.
# The $_ parameter is monomorphic (typed Any) -- let-generalization does not
# polymorphize it because it is a lambda parameter, not a let-binding.
# The [call $identity $_.age] wrapper scopes the WRAP-CALL to the inner call,
# producing a lambda that $map receives as its function argument.
[map [identity _.age] [0: [age: 30] 1: [age: 25]]]
===
Dict({0: Int(30), 1: Int(25)})
